## Unresolved

The new independent-label predicate requires non-overlapping equation projection
rows. That is sufficient for the synthetic offset-label contract examples, but
too conservative for these scans: p72/p73 label glyphs overlap equation ink
vertically, so the new branch does not recover the eight reviewer-confirmed
events. Numerical centre-distance probes also show crowded p66 labels in nearby
distance ranges; they are diagnostic observations, not a validated classifier.
This attempt does not establish that a reliable broader pixel classifier is
impossible. Further implementation work is required before these pages can pass.

